Lower is better. Synthetic data; 20 randomized optimization starts, validation selection, and an untouched test set.

The Bayesian absence test also distinguished a reliable listener from an unreliable one. Under the illustrative assumptions, no detected bark reduced the intruder probability from 20% to 3.85% with reliable hearing, but only to 17.3% with poor hearing.

This demonstrates why expectation and observability matter. It doesn’t establish that any particular real-world silence was intentional.

